  "task": "Write Python 3 function solve(rows). First apply an audit filter to the ORIGINAL input positions, indexed from zero: omit positions whose index modulo 4 equals 1, except always retain the last input position. Rotate the retained rows LEFT by 1 positions modulo the retained length (empty stays empty). Apply the following rules to that transformed list: Parse log rows \"key|integer|status\". Keys contain letters only. Status is OK or VOID. Ignore VOID; for each key keep the LAST OK value, even if zero or negative. Return sorted [key,value] lists.\nReturn the requested value, without printing. Inputs follow the types specified. Do not mutate the input. Standard library is allowed.",
  "specification": "First apply an audit filter to the ORIGINAL input positions, indexed from zero: omit positions whose index modulo 4 equals 1, except always retain the last input position. Rotate the retained rows LEFT by 1 positions modulo the retained length (empty stays empty). Apply the following rules to that transformed list: Parse log rows \"key|integer|status\". Keys contain letters only. Status is OK or VOID. Ignore VOID; for each key keep the LAST OK value, even if zero or negative. Return sorted [key,value] lists.",
  "reference": "def solve(rows):\n d={}\n for row in rows:\n  k,v,s=row.split('|')\n  if s=='OK': d[k]=int(v)\n return [[k,v] for k,v in sorted(d.items())]\n_core_solve=solve\ndef solve(rows):\n filtered=[row for i,row in enumerate(rows) if i%4!=1 or i==len(rows)-1]\n if filtered:\n  shift=1%len(filtered)\n  filtered=filtered[shift:]+filtered[:shift]\n return _core_solve(filtered)",
  "mutation": "def solve(rows):\n d={}\n for row in rows:\n  k,v,s=row.split('|')\n  if s=='OK' and int(v): d[k]=int(v)\n return [[k,v] for k,v in sorted(d.items())]\n_core_solve=solve\ndef solve(rows):\n filtered=[row for i,row in enumerate(rows) if i%4!=1 or i==len(rows)-1]\n if filtered:\n  shift=1%len(filtered)\n  filtered=filtered[shift:]+filtered[:shift]\n return _core_solve(filtered)",
